This is a known breaking change. In .NET 10 (targeting Android 15 / API 35), **edge-to-edge is enforced**, which means `adjustResize` is effectively ignored. You now need to react to **WindowInsets** instead.

### The Fix

In your `Platforms/Android/MainActivity.cs`, use `ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener` to detect the IME (keyboard) inset and apply bottom padding:

```csharp
using Android.Views;
using AndroidX.Core.View;
using Microsoft.Maui;

public class MainActivity : MauiAppCompatActivity
{
    protected override void OnCreate(Android.OS.Bundle? savedInstanceState)
    {
        base.OnCreate(savedInstanceState);

        var rootView = Window!.DecorView.FindViewById(Android.Resource.Id.Content)!;

        ViewCompat.SetOnApplyWindowInsetsListener(rootView, new InsetsListener());
    }

    private class InsetsListener : Java.Lang.Object, IOnApplyWindowInsetsListener
    {
        public WindowInsetsCompat OnApplyWindowInsets(Android.Views.View v, WindowInsetsCompat insets)
        {
            var imeInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime());
            var navInsets = insets.GetInsets(WindowInsetsCompat.Type.NavigationBars());

            // Use the larger of IME or nav-bar bottom inset
            int bottom = Math.Max(imeInsets.Bottom, navInsets.Bottom);

            v.SetPadding(0, 0, 0, bottom);

            return insets;
        }
    }
}
```

### Why this works

| .NET 9 (adjustResize) | .NET 10 (edge-to-edge) |
|---|---|
| OS resized the window for you | Window is always full-screen; you handle insets |
| `WindowSoftInputModeAdjust.Resize` | `WindowInsetsCompat.Type.Ime()` gives keyboard height |

### Also make sure

1. **Remove** any old `adjustResize` configuration (e.g. `Application.UseWindowSoftInputModeAdjust` or manifest entries) — it's a no-op now and can cause confusion.
2. If your chat input is inside a `ScrollView`, ensure the scroll programmatically scrolls to the bottom when the inset changes.
3. On **iOS**, `KeyboardAutoManagerScroll` (enabled by default in MAUI) usually handles this — no extra work needed.
